N=2: double-sum route = -2   published = -2   diff = 0   PASS (exact 0)
N=3: double-sum route = 7*sqrt(2)*sqrt(pi)/4   published = 7*sqrt(2)*sqrt(pi)/4   diff = 0   PASS (exact 0)
N=4: double-sum route = -34/3   published = -34/3   diff = 0   PASS (exact 0)

=> Independent re-derivation (via the FULL double-index Watson's-lemma
   bookkeeping, not merely asserting the telescoping identity) reproduces
   the record's published 4-term law EXACTLY, symbolically, at every one
   of N=1..4. This confirms the target's compressed Sec 2.3 presentation
   (which asserts, rather than shows step-by-step, that R^{(N-1)}(0) factors
   out of the n-sum) is mathematically CORRECT -- the missing intermediate
   step (why R^{(n-1+j)}(0) = R^{(N-1)}(0) independent of n) checks out
